# Git converts LF to CRLF on checkout for Windows users (core.autocrlf), so a fresh clone does not
# contain the bytes the index does. Tests that read tracked files back and match multi-line text
# therefore passed in the worktree they were written in and failed on every clean clone -- three
# migration tests in apps/hub/test/session-eviction.test.ts did exactly that. Pinning the checkout
# to LF makes a clone byte-identical to the index on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# cmd.exe is the one consumer that genuinely wants CRLF, and these launchers are its entry points.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Binaries must never be line-ending converted or diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
